// and a view — is exactly what a direct structuredClone produces. A paired
// walk of the original and the clone records an original-to-clone identity
// map along the edges the clone retained. The second stage walks the
// original again and restores only the own enumerable properties the clone
// discarded — which, at reception-fidelity, can only be content a successful
// form added afterwards (a defaulted field on a Date/RegExp/DataView/…, with
// the fresh plain parent objects a multi-level default created). Those
